**Technique**
1. `POST https://review.keplerops.test/api/review-jobs` with basic auth `rowan.ito:<fk_developer token>`.
2. Key trick: `support_input` must be the bare retained reference `buildops://reviews/diagnostic-request-reference@3` (not the full v3 input object, which returns `build_operations_entitlement_required`).
3. `diagnostic: {profile:"runner-command", argv:["/bin/sh","-c","<script>"]}` runs in worker `fieldlink-review` as `fieldkest-runner`.
4. Worker per-run config lives at `$FIELDLINK_RUN_DIR` (`/tmp/fk-run-RJ-*/fieldlink-ci`), containing `connections.env` + `build-records.curl`.
5. Read `/srv/fieldlink-ci/runner/runner-operations.md`, run the documented build-records connection check (`/api/build-records/worker-status`, principal `svc-fieldlink-ci`).
6. The service awards K09.4 after two distinct runner-command runs: one reading the protected note, another making the authenticated build-records request. After that, runner-command results include the flag.

